# Baz PR review

The user uses **Baz** on GitHub to review pull requests.

When a PR is up and Baz has finished (or the user asks to look at Baz’s review):

1. Read Baz’s comments on the PR (`gh` / review comments).
2. Ignore suggestions that are not relevant to the work we actually did (style bikeshedding, speculative refactors, unrelated architecture, scope expansion).
3. Keep the ones that catch real errors, regressions, missed edge cases, a11y bugs, or details we overlooked. Baz is strong at those.
4. **Print those items** in the chat. Do not start fixing them.
5. Wait. Discuss with the user. They will approve items or give guidance, then we update.

Never apply Baz’s recommendations automatically.
